Part 1: Single-Asset Valuation

The valuation engine is a sequential pipeline. Each model produces a structured output that feeds the next model.

Full current flow:

```text
DrugAssetProgram / YAML config
  -> ValuationEngine.from_program()
  -> POS Layer 1
  -> POS Layer 2 trial-design adjustment
  -> ProbabilityModel
  -> RevenueModel
  -> CostModel
  -> RNPVModel
  -> NAV/share
  -> scenarios, Monte Carlo, sensitivity, market expectation, M&A artifacts
```

The valuation engine does not produce a single opaque score. It produces a value bridge:

| Layer | Question answered | Main output |
|---|---|---|
| POS Layer 1 | How strong is the asset evidence relative to base rates? | Adjusted phase POS |
| POS Layer 2 | Is the trial/regulatory design credible? | Design-adjusted phase POS |
| Probability | What is cumulative probability of approval? | `cumulative_approval_probability` |
| Revenue | What sales/EBIT could the drug generate if approved? | Annual revenue and EBIT streams |
| Cost | What development/deal obligations must be funded? | `total_pv_weighted_millions` |
| rNPV | What is the risk-adjusted asset value? | `rnpv_millions` |
| NAV/share | What is equity value per diluted share? | `nav_per_share` |
| Variant perception | What is the market implying? | Implied POS / implied sales / POS gap |
| Scenario / Monte Carlo | How wide is the range of outcomes? | Bull/base/bear and percentile distribution |

