Step 2 — POS Layer 2: Trial Design / Regulatory Evidence Quality

Status: Implemented.

Layer 1 scores what the evidence says.
Layer 2 scores whether the evidence package is trustworthy and regulator-acceptable.

Current module:

`src/bve/models/trial_design_features.py`

Current concepts:

| Component | What it measures |
|---|---|
| Evidence design quality | Trial robustness and evidence grade |
| Comparator fit | Whether control arm / standard of care choice is credible |
| Regulatory pathway risk | Whether FDA/EMA path is realistic |
| Phase scaling | Makes design adjustment smaller in early phases and larger in pivotal settings |

General formula:

```text
design_adjustment =
    evidence_quality_adjustment
  + comparator_fit_adjustment
  + regulatory_pathway_adjustment
  + other_design_penalties_or_bonuses

phase_scaled_adjustment = design_adjustment * phase_weight

final_design_adjustment = clip(phase_scaled_adjustment, lower_cap, upper_cap)
```

Current phase scaling:

| Phase | Relative design impact |
|---|---:|
| Phase 1 | 0.20 |
| Phase 2 | 0.50 |
| Phase 3 | 1.00 |
| NDA/BLA | 0.90 |

Important limitation:

Layer 2 currently separates design quality from endpoint/biology conceptually, but anti-double-counting is not a full
institutional audit system. Analysts still need to check that endpoint strength, comparator quality, and regulatory path
are not rewarded twice.

