Step 3 — Cumulative Approval Probability

Status: Implemented.

After each remaining phase has a success probability, the probability model computes:

```text
P(reaching phase_i) = product(success_probability_j for all prior phases j)

P(approval) = product(success_probability_i for all remaining phases i)
```

Example:

```text
P(approval) for Phase 2 asset =
    P(pass Phase 2)
  × P(pass Phase 3 | Phase 2 success)
  × P(pass NDA/BLA | Phase 3 success)
```

Why this matters:

A Phase 2 asset can have a reasonable chance of a positive Phase 2 readout but still have a much lower cumulative
probability of approval because Phase 3 and filing risk remain.

Current outputs include:

| Output | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `prob_reaching` by phase | Probability the asset survives to that phase |
| `years_to_approval` | Sum of remaining phase durations |
| `cumulative_approval_probability` | Probability used by rNPV commercial cash flows |

