Step 4 — Revenue Model

Status: Implemented.

The revenue model projects annual sales from launch through patent expiry and post-LOE erosion. It is deliberately
separate from probability; revenue is the "if approved" commercial stream.

Supported market-sizing modes:

| Mode | Best use | Current status |
|---|---|---|
| Patient-based sizing | Most diligence-grade single-asset models | Implemented |
| Line-of-therapy segmentation | Oncology and staged treatment settings | Implemented |
| TAM-based sizing | Early rough screens | Implemented |
| Hybrid commercial inputs | Patient funnel + price + geography + access + competition | Implemented |

Patient-based formula:

```text
eligible_patients =
    population
  × prevalence_or_incidence
  × diagnosed_rate
  × eligible_rate
  × treatment_rate
  × line_of_therapy_share

treated_patients_t =
    eligible_patients
  × penetration_t
  × payer_access_multiplier_t
  × geography_launch_multiplier_t
  × competition_multiplier_t

net_price_t =
    list_or_WAC_price_t
  × (1 - gross_to_net_discount_t)
  × pre_LOE_price_erosion_t

revenue_t =
    treated_patients_t
  × net_price_t
  × treatment_duration_factor
```

EBIT formula:

```text
gross_profit_t = revenue_t * gross_margin_t
SG&A_t = revenue_t * SG&A_rate_t
EBIT_t = revenue_t - COGS_t - SG&A_t
```

Current revenue features:

| Feature | Current status | Why it matters |
|---|---|---|
| Gross-to-net pricing | Implemented | Avoids using unrealistic list-price revenue |
| Pre-LOE price erosion | Implemented | Captures net price decline before patent expiry |
| Launch archetypes | Implemented | Models different launch shapes |
| Fractional ex-US launch delays | Implemented | Avoids crude whole-year snapping |
| Geography split | Implemented | Supports US, EU5, Japan, China, ROW-style rollout |
| Payer access | Implemented | Access probability, delay, PA burden, step edit |
| Competition | Implemented | Share and price erosion effects |
| COGS by modality | Implemented | Different economics for small molecule, biologic, gene/cell, ADC, RNA |
| SG&A by commercial model | Implemented | Self-commercialized vs partnered vs royalty-only economics |
| LOE erosion | Implemented | Post-patent tail by modality/config |

Revenue model limitation:

The code can express detailed assumptions, but it does not prove the assumptions are correct. Patient counts, penetration,
net price, payer access, and competitor erosion remain analyst-owned inputs.

