Step 5 — Cost Model

Status: Implemented.

The cost model is a stateless engine that converts outgoing development/deal obligations into probability-weighted present
value. It returns `CostStream`, which is then subtracted by `RNPVModel`.

Five categories:

1. Trial R&D
2. CMC/manufacturing
3. Payable milestones
4. Upfront costs
5. Post-approval commitments

Category 1 — Trial R&D:

```text
cost_after_share_i = phase_cost_i × cdev_cost_share

PV_gross_i =
    cost_after_share_i
  × (1 + cost_inflation_rate)^t
  / (1 + discount_rate)^t

PV_weighted_i =
    PV_gross_i × P(reaching phase_i)
```

Default timing:

```text
t = (phase_start + phase_end) / 2
```

If `ANNUAL_UNIFORM` spend profile is used, the tool splits spending into year segments and discounts each segment at its
own midpoint.

Category 2 — CMC/manufacturing:

```text
CMC_total =
    api_development
  + formulation
  + manufacturing_scale_up
  + regulatory_cmc

PV_CMC =
    CMC_total / (1 + discount_rate)^anchor_year
  × probability_weight
```

CMC timing modes:

| Mode | Discount anchor |
|---|---|
| `parallel_to_phase_3` | Phase 3 midpoint |
| `post_phase_2` | Phase 2 end |
| `pre_phase_3_start` | Phase 3 start |
| `custom_year` | Analyst-specified year |

Probability weight is normally `P(reaching Phase 3)`. If no Phase 3 is present, it falls back to the last phase's
`prob_reaching`.

Category 3 — Payable milestones:

```text
PV_milestone_i =
    amount_i / (1 + discount_rate)^trigger_year_i
  × trigger_probability_i
```

Trigger logic:

| Trigger | Timing | Probability weight |
|---|---|---|
| `PHASE_START` | Phase start | `P(reaching phase)` |
| `PHASE_SUCCESS` | Phase end | `P(reaching phase) × phase_success_probability` |
| `APPROVAL` | Years to approval | Cumulative approval probability |
| `FIRST_SALE` | Approval year + launch offset | Cumulative approval probability |
| `SALES_THRESHOLD` | First year revenue exceeds threshold | Cumulative approval probability; requires revenue stream |

Important boundary:

`CostModel` does not own revenue. Sales-threshold payable milestones that need a revenue stream are resolved in the rNPV
path when revenue is available.

Category 4 — Upfront costs:

```text
PV_upfront_cost = upfront_cost_millions
```

No discounting and no probability weighting because it is a time-zero cash outflow.

Category 5 — Post-approval commitments:

```text
PV_post_approval =
    post_approval_rd_millions
  / (1 + discount_rate)^years_to_approval
  × P(approval)
```

Aggregation:

```text
total_pv_weighted_development_costs =
    Σ PV_weighted(trial_R&D)
  + PV_CMC
  + Σ PV_weighted(payable_milestones)
  + upfront_cost
  + PV_post_approval
```

Boundary:

Royalties and profit shares are not treated as development costs. Revenue is gross commercial revenue; deal royalties and
profit shares are deducted in `RNPVModel`.

