Step 6 — rNPV / NAV

Status: Implemented.

Core rNPV equation:

```text
rNPV =
    P(approval)
  × Σ [ after_tax_FCF_t × net_ownership / (1 + WACC)^t ]
  - total_pv_weighted_development_costs
  + PV(receivable_milestones)
  + upfront_receipts
```

Per-year bridge:

```text
royalty_t = revenue_t × deal.royalty_rate
profit_share_t = EBIT_t × deal.profit_share_rate

adjusted_EBIT_t =
    EBIT_t
  - royalty_t
  - profit_share_t

cash_tax_t =
    tax_model(adjusted_EBIT_t, NOLs, jurisdiction mix)

after_tax_FCF_t =
    adjusted_EBIT_t
  - cash_tax_t
  - maintenance_capex_t
  - working_capital_t
  - launch_capex_t
```

Tax paths:

| Path | When used | Behavior |
|---|---|---|
| Simple tax path | No `TaxProfile` | Applies simple NOL benefit years and effective tax rate |
| `TaxProfile` path | `TaxProfile` supplied | Tracks NOL usage, blended or US/ex-US tax rate, capex, working capital |

NAV:

```text
NAV =
    asset_rNPV
  + net_cash
  - debt
  - corporate_overhead_PV
  + other_adjustments

NAV/share =
    NAV / diluted_shares_outstanding
```

Interpretation:

| Output | How to read it |
|---|---|
| rNPV | Risk-adjusted value of the asset economics |
| NAV/share | Equity value estimate after company balance sheet and share count |
| Probability-adjusted revenue PV | Commercial value after approval probability |
| PV development costs | Obligations deducted from value |
| Royalty/profit-share PV | Deal economics reducing captured value |

Known limits:

| Limit | Why it matters |
|---|---|
| Purchase accounting not modeled | M&A tax amortization/step-up can matter |
| Section 382 not deeply modeled | NOL usability after ownership change can change |
| Royalty stacks depend on config | Exact contract terms are not automatically parsed |
| Diluted share count must be current | NAV/share can be wrong after financings |

