Step 7 — Scenario Analysis

Status: Implemented.

Base scenario engine:

| Scenario | Peak sales | POS | Timing | Cost | WACC |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Bull | 1.50× | 1.30× | Faster | 0.90× | Lower |
| Base | 1.00× | 1.00× | Base | 1.00× | Base |
| Bear | 0.55× | 0.70× | Slower | 1.20× | Higher |

Shock categories:

| Category | Examples |
|---|---|
| Clinical | POS changes, endpoint miss, safety issues |
| Regulatory | CRL/delay, pathway changes |
| Commercial | Price, access, penetration, geography |
| Competition | Competitor approval/success, price erosion |
| Cost | Trial, CMC, inflation |
| Deal economics | Royalties, milestones, profit share |

Scenario output is useful for:

1. Understanding downside if the base case is wrong.
2. Showing which variable drives value.
3. Framing catalyst payoff.
4. Testing kill criteria.

