Step 8 — Monte Carlo

Status: Implemented.

Monte Carlo modes:

| Mode | What it samples |
|---|---|
| Simple | POS, peak sales, discount rate |
| Driver-based | Eligible patients, price, penetration, payer/geography factors, costs, timing, competitors |

Variables sampled include:

| Variable | Typical distribution approach |
|---|---|
| Phase success probabilities | Beta-style uncertainty around POS |
| Peak sales | Lognormal |
| Discount rate | Normal clipped to bounds |
| Years to peak | Normal/rounded/clipped |
| Phase duration | Gamma-style timing uncertainty |
| Trial costs | Lognormal |
| Financing dilution | Scenario distribution |
| Competitor outcomes | Sampled competitor state |

Important guardrail:

The engine validates against direct peak-sales sampling plus driver-level sales sampling when that would double-count
commercial uncertainty.

Interpretation:

| Output | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Mean | Average simulated rNPV |
| Median | Central case less sensitive to outliers |
| P10/P90 | Downside/upside range |
| Probability positive | Fraction of simulations with positive rNPV |
| VaR/downside | Tail-risk framing |
| Variance drivers | Which assumptions explain distribution width |

