Step 9 — Variant Perception / Market-Implied Expectations

Status: Implemented.

Purpose:

Compare model assumptions with what the public market appears to imply.

General formulas:

```text
enterprise_value =
    market_cap
  + debt
  - cash

isolated_asset_EV =
    enterprise_value
  - value_of_non_target_assets
  - residual_platform_value

market_implied_POS =
    isolated_asset_EV / probability_unadjusted_asset_value

POS_gap =
    model_POS - market_implied_POS
```

Interpretation:

| Result | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Model POS > implied POS | Model is more optimistic than market |
| Model POS < implied POS | Market is more optimistic than model |
| Implied POS > 100% | Asset isolation or non-target value likely wrong |
| Implied POS < 0% | EV/cash/non-target adjustments likely wrong |

This is a diagnostic, not a true market survey. It can be distorted by short interest, financing risk, index flows,
non-target assets, platform value, and stale market data.

