---
M&A Step 0 — Acquisition Screen

Status: Implemented.

Purpose:

Identify whether a target is cheap or attractive enough to merit acquisition analysis.

Key formula:

```text
enterprise_value = market_cap - net_cash

acquisition_discount =
    model_asset_rNPV / enterprise_value
```

Critical guardrail:

The acquisition screen does not multiply by probability of approval again. rNPV is already probability-adjusted. Multiplying
again would double-count clinical risk.

Main outputs:

| Output | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Enterprise value | Market value of operating assets net of cash |
| Model rNPV | Model's risk-adjusted value estimate |
| Acquisition discount | How much model value exceeds EV |
| Model POS | Probability already embedded in rNPV |
| Readiness flags | Whether asset is plausibly acquisition-ready |

Limit:

Acquisition discount is a screen, not a deal thesis. A high discount can mean undervaluation, but it can also mean the model
is missing rights issues, bad data, weak demand, financing stress, or clinical risk.

---
M&A Step 1 — Acquisition Readiness

Status: Implemented.

Purpose:

Prevent immature or weakly de-risked assets from ranking as acquisition-ready simply because they are cheap.

Current logic:

| Stage / evidence | Treatment |
|---|---|
| Phase 3 or later | Generally acquisition-ready |
| Preclinical / Phase 1 | Generally not ready |
| Phase 2 | Requires evidence: readout, endpoint success, adequate design, posterior POS improvement |

Why it matters:

Biotech acquirers usually do not buy every cheap Phase 1 asset. They buy assets when evidence, timing, strategic need, and
deal setup align.

---
M&A Step 2 — Comparable Deals

Status: Implemented.

Purpose:

Benchmark target value against precedent deals.

Matching hierarchy:

| Match level | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Exact canonical indication + phase | Highest-quality comp |
| Therapeutic area + phase | Broader but still relevant |
| Phase-only | Weak fallback |

Outputs:

| Output | Meaning |
|---|---|
| EV / peak sales band | Precedent valuation range |
| Peer min / median / max | Comparable-deal distribution |
| Fair value band | Implied acquisition value range |
| Premium / discount | Whether target appears cheap/rich vs comps |
| High-quality band | Uses better-matched comps when available |

Limit:

Comparable deals can be misleading when headline biobucks are confused with upfront value, when rights differ, or when
platform value is mixed with asset value.

