M&A Step 3 — Acquirer Fit

Status: Implemented.

Purpose:

Score whether a specific buyer is a logical owner for a target.

Core inputs:

| Input | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Therapeutic area fit | Does buyer operate in this disease area? |
| Modality fit | Does buyer understand/develop/manufacture this modality? |
| Stage fit | Does buyer buy assets at this stage? |
| Strategic priority | Does target match stated priorities / gaps? |
| Valuation / budget | Is deal size plausible? |
| Existing partnership | Does buyer already have relationship/control? |

General acquirer-fit formula family:

```text
fit_score =
    w_TA × therapeutic_area_score
  + w_modality × modality_score
  + w_stage × stage_score
  + w_priority × strategic_priority_score
  + w_valuation × valuation_score
  + w_budget × budget_score
  + partnership_bonus
  - hard_fail_penalties
```

Current hard fails:

| Hard fail | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Pre-Phase 2 stage | Too early for many acquirers |
| Not acquisition-ready | Evidence quality insufficient |
| Outside budget | Deal size implausible for buyer |

Important current limitation:

Acquirer profiles are curated YAML/profile data. They can encode pipeline gaps, modality preferences, priorities, budget,
recent deals, and partnerships, but they are only as fresh and complete as the research inputs.

