M&A Step 4 — Live M&A Probability Scanner

Status: Implemented, validation limited.

Current module:

`src/bve/intelligence/ma_probability.py`

Current score versions:

| Version | Main behavior |
|---|---|
| v1.0 | Acquisition discount + strategic fit + de-risking + capital vulnerability |
| v1.1 | Similar, with valuation component mode changes |
| v1.2 | Strategic-fit-only style stress version |
| v1.3 | Strategic fit + scarcity |
| v1.4 | Strategic fit + de-risking + capital vulnerability + scarcity |

Default config currently defines `score_version="v1.2"` unless overridden.

Current v1.4 formula:

```text
raw_mna_score =
    0.00 × acquisition_discount_component
  + 0.65 × strategic_fit_score
  + 0.20 × de_risking_stage_score
  + 0.05 × capital_vulnerability_score
  + 0.10 × scarcity_score
```

Earlier versions can include acquisition discount directly. The config controls which score version is used.

Component details:

| Component | Current logic |
|---|---|
| Valuation discount score | Buckets acquisition discount into 0.1-1.0 score |
| Strategic fit score | Urgency-adjusted TA + modality + strategic priority + budget, with penalties and cap |
| De-risking score | Stage/readiness bucket plus design/POS quality modifiers |
| Capital vulnerability | Cash runway, target vulnerability signals, external deal pressure |
| Scarcity | Peer count, stage eligibility, TA competition modifiers |

Valuation discount bucket:

| Acquisition discount | Score |
|---|---:|
| >= 3.0x | 1.00 |
| >= 2.5x | 0.90 |
| >= 2.0x | 0.80 |
| >= 1.5x | 0.70 |
| >= 1.2x | 0.55 |
| >= 1.0x | 0.40 |
| >= 0.75x | 0.25 |
| < 0.75x | 0.10 |

Strategic fit current mechanics:

```text
strategic_base =
    urgency_multiplier × TA_component
  + modality_component
  + strategic_priority_component
  + budget_component

strategic_fit =
    min(
      strategic_base / strategic_weight
      + BD_pattern_adjustment
      - quality_penalties,
      strategic_fit_hard_cap
    )
```

Current hard cap:

```text
strategic_fit_hard_cap = 0.70
```

Strategic penalties:

| Penalty | Trigger |
|---|---|
| Weak commercial overlap | TA score < 0.50 |
| Poor modality fit | Modality score < 0.50 |
| No pipeline gap | Strategic priority < 0.50 |
| Poor deal-size fit | Budget score < 0.40 |

Gap urgency multipliers:

| Urgency | Multiplier |
|---|---:|
| High | 1.00 |
| Medium | 0.55 |
| Low | 0.28 |
| No matched gap | 0.15 |

BD pattern adjustment:

| Pattern | Adjustment |
|---|---:|
| 3+ recent deals | +0.03 |
| 0 recent deals | -0.12 |

De-risking score:

| Bucket / stage | Base score |
|---|---:|
| Phase 3 or later | 0.62 |
| Phase 2 proof-of-concept | 0.50 |
| Phase 2 pre-proof-of-concept | 0.30 |
| Pre-Phase 2 | 0.08 |
| Unknown | 0.20 |

Additional modifiers:

| Modifier | Effect |
|---|---:|
| OS RCT design tier | +0.08 |
| PFS design tier | +0.04 |
| Surrogate endpoint | -0.12 |
| Single-arm | -0.20 |
| Posterior POS > prior POS | Up to +0.10 |
| Low power | -0.15 |
| Safety overhang | -0.12 |
| Prior Phase 3 failure | -0.18 |
| Label uncertainty | -0.08 |
| Prior Phase 2 failure | -0.10 |
| Regulatory risk | -0.08 |
| Endpoint in dispute | -0.07 |
| Breakthrough designation | +0.06 |

Current cap:

```text
de_risking_stage_score <= 0.80
```

Transaction-likelihood gates in live scanner:

| Gate | Trigger | Cap |
|---|---|---:|
| No transaction trigger | No financing, deal activity, catalyst, activist, or valuation-distress trigger | 0.55 |
| Dual low-pressure gate | Financing pressure < 0.25 and external deal activity < 0.20 | 0.55 |
| High-score two-driver requirement | Score > 0.75 with fewer than two drivers | 0.75 |

Transaction drivers:

| Driver | Threshold |
|---|---:|
| Financing pressure | >= 0.35 |
| External deal activity | >= 0.30 |
| Catalyst proximity | Catalyst within 90 days |
| Activist / target signal | >= 0.30 |
| Valuation distress | Valuation discount >= 0.45 and de-risking >= 0.50 |

Final live scanner flow:

```text
raw_mna_score
  -> saturation_penalty
  -> transaction_likelihood_gate
  -> targetability_multiplier
  -> hard_fail_zeroing if targetability hard fail
  -> best acquirer selected
  -> target rows sorted by score
  -> optional calibration overlay fields
```

Interpretation:

The live M&A score is a ranking score. It should not be read as a fully calibrated takeout probability unless a calibrated
model and adequate label base are explicitly present.

