M&A Step 9 — Institutional Layer 5 Calibration Overlay

Status: Implemented as standalone module; empirical validation still limited.

Current module:

`src/bve/intelligence/ma_layer5_calibration.py`

Purpose:

Convert a post-gate rank score into a time-bounded probability estimate with confidence, uncertainty, and explanations.

Logistic transform:

```text
logistic_probability =
    sigmoid(8.0 × (rank_score - 0.68))
```

Approximate mapping:

| Rank score | Logistic probability |
|---:|---:|
| 0.35 | ~7% |
| 0.55 | ~26% |
| 0.70 | ~54% |
| 0.80 | ~72% |

Shrinkage:

```text
p_takeout_12m =
    w_base × base_rate
  + w_logistic × logistic_probability
  + w_bucket × comparable_bucket_rate
```

Shrinkage weights:

| Comparable N | Base rate | Logistic | Bucket |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| < 10 | 60% | 20% | 20% |
| 10-19 | 50% | 30% | 20% |
| 20-29 | 40% | 40% | 20% |
| >= 30 | 30% | 50% | 20% |

Time windows:

```text
p_takeout_6m  ≈ p_takeout_12m × 0.55
p_takeout_18m ≈ 1 - (1 - p_takeout_12m)^1.35
```

Probability bands:

| Band | Range |
|---|---:|
| Very low | < 5% |
| Low | 5-15% |
| Moderate | 15-30% |
| High | 30-50% |
| Exceptional / manual review | > 50% |

Correct interpretation:

Layer 5 helps communicate probability responsibly, but the probability is only as credible as the historical takeout/control
dataset. With sparse labels, bands and confidence language are more trustworthy than exact decimals.

