Part 3: How Valuation Feeds M&A

Valuation outputs become M&A inputs as follows:

| Valuation output | M&A use |
|---|---|
| rNPV | Core estimate of asset value |
| Enterprise value | Price buyer must pay before premium |
| Acquisition discount | Model value vs public market value |
| Peak sales | Commercial attractiveness and comparable-deal multiple |
| POS / de-risking | Acquisition-readiness and stage score |
| Cost-to-complete | Buyer funding burden and seller financing pressure |
| Scenario downside | Deal risk / walk-away price |
| Monte Carlo distribution | Uncertainty and tail risk |
| Market-implied POS | Investor disagreement / valuation dislocation |

Example bridge:

```text
expected_acquisition_price =
    enterprise_value × (1 + takeout_premium)

premium_adjusted_rnpv_gap =
    model_rnpv
  - expected_acquisition_price
  - remaining_cost_to_complete
  + buyer_specific_synergy_value

acquisition_discount =
    model_rnpv / enterprise_value
```

Interpretation:

| Situation | M&A implication |
|---|---|
| High rNPV, low EV, good evidence | Potential undervalued acquisition target |
| High rNPV, high EV | Strategic fit matters more than cheapness |
| Low rNPV, high financing pressure | Distress alone; should not rank highly |
| High peak sales, weak rights | May be license/option, not full acquisition |
| Strong fit, no seller willingness | Strategic radar / relationship build |
| Strong seller pressure, weak asset | Pass or distressed optionality cap |

---
Part 4: Worked Example

Assume:

- Phase 2 asset.
- Model rNPV = $1.2B.
- Target enterprise value = $500M.
- Expected takeout premium = 60%.
- Remaining cost-to-complete = $250M.
- Buyer has high TA fit but no existing relationship.
- Seller has 4 quarters of runway and a catalyst in 9 months.

Valuation bridge:

```text
expected_acquisition_price =
    $500M × 1.60 = $800M

premium_adjusted_gap =
    $1.2B - $800M - $250M = $150M

acquisition_discount =
    $1.2B / $500M = 2.4x
```

M&A interpretation:

| Signal | Read |
|---|---|
| Positive premium-adjusted gap | Deal can create value after premium and development cost |
| 2.4x acquisition discount | Public EV is below model value |
| Phase 2 stage | Needs proof-of-concept quality review |
| 4 quarters runway | Financing pressure may create transaction window |
| Catalyst in 9 months | Could be pre-data option or post-data acquisition setup |
| No relationship | Right-to-win may be lower than a partner acquirer |

Possible routing:

| Additional fact | Likely route |
|---|---|
| Clean rights, high buyer urgency | Active pursuit / catalyst watch |
| Encumbered rights | Option/license/relationship build |
| Weak clinical evidence | Gate-capped or pass |
| Seller raises capital | Strategic radar |
| Buyer has internal failure in same TA | Higher pipeline-gap urgency |

