The current tool is much more advanced than a simple rNPV spreadsheet or basic M&A heat map, but several institutional gaps
remain.

| Area | Current status | Why it matters |
|---|---|---|
| POS calibration | Implemented, validation limited | POS drives valuation error |
| Commercial assumptions | Implemented/config-driven | Peak sales can dominate value |
| Rights/control | Partial | Can block full acquisition |
| Exact royalty stacks | Partial/config-driven | Can destroy economics |
| Regional rights | Missing / needed | Determines structure and value |
| Change-of-control clauses | Missing / needed | Can trigger payments or consent rights |
| Antitrust | Placeholder/partial | Strategic overlap can reduce feasibility |
| Seller willingness | Partial | Fit does not imply transaction |
| Acquirer profile freshness | Config-driven | Buyer strategy changes quickly |
| Pair-level calibration | Partial | Needed for credible probability outputs |
| Deal structure probability | Implemented routing, validation limited | BD cares about structure, not just takeout |

